[{"text": "I now give the floor to his highness", "start": 1.12, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "prince faal bin farhan al-saw,", "start": 3.919, "duration": 7.521}, {"text": "minister for foreign affairs of Saudi", "start": 8.24, "duration": 6.2}, {"text": "Arabia.", "start": 11.44, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "In the name of God the most gracious,", "start": 35.44, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "the most merciful, your majesties,", "start": 37.36, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "excellencies and highnesses, Mr.", "start": 39.44, "duration": 3.439}, {"text": "President of the United Nations General", "start": 41.12, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "Assembly, Mr. Secretary General,", "start": 42.879, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "distinguished guests, peace, mercy, and", "start": 45.28, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "blessings of God be upon you. At the", "start": 47.68, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "outset, we wish to congratulate his", "start": 50.16, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "excellency Mr. Rahman on his election as", "start": 52.16, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "president of the 81st session of the", "start": 54.48, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "United Nations General Assembly. We wish", "start": 57.199, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "him every success in guiding the work of", "start": 59.52, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "this session. We also wish to express", "start": 61.76, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "our thanks to Mrs. Analina Burbach for", "start": 64.4, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "her efforts during her presidency of the", "start": 66.799, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "81st session of the GA. We further", "start": 68.799, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "express our profound thanks and", "start": 71.52, "duration": 2.88}, {"text": "appreciation to his excellency Mr.", "start": 72.96, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "Antonia Geres, Secretary General of the", "start": 74.4, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "United Nations for his continued effort", "start": 76.56, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "in furthering the purposes of the UN.", "start": 78.72, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "Mr. President, the work of the session", "start": 81.119, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "is taking place at a time when the world", "start": 82.72, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "and the multilateral system are facing", "start": 84.479, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "rapidly evolving and unprecedented", "start": 86.88, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "challenges. While crisis and conflicts", "start": 89.439, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "continue in many parts of the world,", "start": 92.0, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "there is an increasing need to uphold", "start": 94.64, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "the principles of the UN charter,", "start": 96.799, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "respect international law, and", "start": 99.04, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "strengthen the effectiveness of", "start": 101.04, "duration": 2.96}, {"text": "international institutions in", "start": 102.64, "duration": 2.72}, {"text": "maintaining international peace and", "start": 104.0, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "security and advancing sustainable", "start": 105.36, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "development.", "start": 107.36, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "Crises arise not so much from an absence", "start": 108.96, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "of resources and opportunities, but", "start": 111.36, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "rather from a lack of commitment to the", "start": 113.28, "duration": 2.879}, {"text": "principles agreed upon by the", "start": 114.96, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "international community. The Kingdom of", "start": 116.159, "duration": 3.761}, {"text": "Saudi Arabia and the countries of the", "start": 118.64, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "region have been subjected to flagrant", "start": 119.92, "duration": 3.519}, {"text": "Iranian attacks targeting their", "start": 121.92, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "security, resources, and civilian and", "start": 123.439, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "economic facilities. The kingdom", "start": 125.28, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "reiterates its full right to protect its", "start": 127.439, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "security and sovereignty, its citizens", "start": 129.84, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "and residents, and its national", "start": 132.0, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "resources. We call upon the", "start": 134.319, "duration": 3.521}, {"text": "international community to shoulder its", "start": 136.239, "duration": 3.281}, {"text": "responsibilities in confronting all", "start": 137.84, "duration": 3.039}, {"text": "threats to international peace and", "start": 139.52, "duration": 3.439}, {"text": "security. The security of the Gulf", "start": 140.879, "duration": 3.601}, {"text": "region is part and parcel of the", "start": 142.959, "duration": 3.441}, {"text": "security of the region and the world at", "start": 144.48, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "large. The stability of this vital", "start": 146.4, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "region is directly linked to global", "start": 148.319, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "energy security, the steadiness of", "start": 150.4, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "international trade and the resilience", "start": 152.56, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "of global supply chains. Mr. President", "start": 154.56, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "safeguarding international navigation", "start": 157.92, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "and the resilience of global supply", "start": 159.68, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "chains is a shared responsibility that", "start": 161.36, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "requires serious international", "start": 164.239, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "cooperation to prevent risks that could", "start": 166.319, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "affect the global economy.", "start": 169.2, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "In this regard, the kingdom stresses the", "start": 172.879, "duration": 3.521}, {"text": "importance of ensuring freedom of", "start": 174.879, "duration": 3.761}, {"text": "navigation in all international", "start": 176.4, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "waterways for most among them the strait", "start": 178.64, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "of harmony", "start": 181.28, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "and the Gulf of Aden. We must restore", "start": 183.519, "duration": 3.681}, {"text": "the situation in the street of harmers", "start": 185.599, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "to its pre-28th of February status", "start": 187.2, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "without the imposition of any fees or", "start": 189.44, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "restrictions. The kingdom rejects the", "start": 191.36, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "use by any party of these vital", "start": 193.2, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "waterways as an instrument of pressure,", "start": 195.04, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "threat or harm to the interests of", "start": 196.959, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "states in accordance with international", "start": 198.8, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "law and relevant UN resolutions. Mr.", "start": 200.879, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "President, efforts to restore security", "start": 203.44, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "and stability in the region and to build", "start": 205.599, "duration": 3.041}, {"text": "sustainable relations among its", "start": 207.2, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "countries cannot be based on domination,", "start": 208.64, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "influence or exploitation of crisis.", "start": 211.68, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "Rather, they must be founded on mutual", "start": 214.08, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "respect, common interests, good", "start": 216.0, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "neighborliness, respect for the", "start": 218.56, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "sovereignty of states and full", "start": 220.08, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "compliance with international law and", "start": 221.92, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "international humanitarian law. In this", "start": 223.92, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "vein, the kingdom supports efforts and", "start": 225.84, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "initiatives that contribute to", "start": 227.76, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "deescalation for most among among them", "start": 229.28, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "the efforts of Qatar, Pakistan and other", "start": 232.0, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "sisterly and friendly countries. This", "start": 234.08, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "would contribute to restoring stability", "start": 236.319, "duration": 3.2}, {"text": "to the region and creating conditions", "start": 237.84, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "conducive to dialogue and diplomacy. We", "start": 239.519, "duration": 3.761}, {"text": "stress the importance of ensuring that", "start": 241.68, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "any arrangements on the regional", "start": 243.28, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "security must be comprehensive,", "start": 245.76, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "effective and sustainable. They must", "start": 247.599, "duration": 3.441}, {"text": "clearly address the root causes of", "start": 249.28, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "threat and instability.", "start": 251.04, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "Um we stress the need to ensure that the", "start": 253.04, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "entire region is free of weapons of mass", "start": 254.959, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "destruction and that peaceful nuclear", "start": 257.199, "duration": 3.921}, {"text": "programs are subject to international", "start": 259.04, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "oversight, verification and safeguards.", "start": 261.12, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "As such, we would enhance confidence and", "start": 263.36, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "safeguard regional and international", "start": 265.12, "duration": 3.359}, {"text": "security.", "start": 266.8, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "the continued suffering of the", "start": 268.479, "duration": 3.921}, {"text": "Palestinian people in the Gaza Strip and", "start": 270.56, "duration": 3.12}, {"text": "the West Bank and the targeting of", "start": 272.4, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "civilians by Israeli occupation, the", "start": 273.68, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "obstruction of humanitarian assistance", "start": 276.08, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "attempts at full state displacement and", "start": 277.919, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "the continued expansion of illegal", "start": 280.08, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "settlements all constitute serious", "start": 282.0, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "violations of international law and", "start": 284.32, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "international humanitarian law.", "start": 286.08, "duration": 7.679}, {"text": "The kingdom uh rejects any attempts at", "start": 289.52, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "force displacement or changing the", "start": 293.759, "duration": 3.041}, {"text": "status quo of the Palestinian", "start": 295.6, "duration": 2.64}, {"text": "territories. We stress that a just and", "start": 296.8, "duration": 2.8}, {"text": "lasting peace can only be achieved", "start": 298.24, "duration": 2.48}, {"text": "through the implementation of a", "start": 299.6, "duration": 3.039}, {"text": "two-state solution and the establishment", "start": 300.72, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "of an independent Palestinian state on", "start": 302.639, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "the 1967 borders with East Jerusalem as", "start": 304.4, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "its capital. The kingdom stresses the", "start": 307.52, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "need to support effort a aimed at", "start": 310.24, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "reaching a comprehensive political", "start": 312.88, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "solution that will ensure the stability", "start": 314.56, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "of Yemen uh and alleviate the suffering", "start": 316.88, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "of those brotherly people. We have", "start": 319.759, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "provided humanitarian and development", "start": 321.52, "duration": 2.88}, {"text": "assistance to the Republic of Yemen,", "start": 323.039, "duration": 3.201}, {"text": "amounting to more than 29 billion US", "start": 324.4, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "dollars. We were the first among", "start": 326.24, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "humanitarian donors to the Republic of", "start": 328.639, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "Yemen in 2025.", "start": 331.36, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "The kingdom in this regard welcomes the", "start": 333.919, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "statement issued by the members of the", "start": 336.16, "duration": 2.96}, {"text": "security council, including the", "start": 337.759, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "condemnation of the missile and drone", "start": 339.12, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "attacks carried out by the Houthi", "start": 341.039, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "terrorist militia against the kingdom", "start": 343.12, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "and against commercial vessels. The", "start": 345.44, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "kingdom calls upon the international", "start": 347.68, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "community to reject and condemn all the", "start": 349.36, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "Houthy terrorists, militias, aggressions", "start": 353.199, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "and um criminal acts that threaten the", "start": 355.759, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "security of navigation in the Red Sea", "start": 358.8, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "and Babandep Strait. With regard to", "start": 360.32, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "Sudan, the kingdom stresses the", "start": 362.72, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "importance of Sudan's stability", "start": 364.08, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "um territorial integrity and unity while", "start": 367.36, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "maintaining its natural resources and", "start": 370.08, "duration": 3.679}, {"text": "institutions. The solution to the crisis", "start": 371.6, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "must be an intraudinis political", "start": 373.759, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "solution that respects the sovereignty", "start": 375.52, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "and unity of Sudan. It must be based on", "start": 377.039, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "supporting Sudin state institutions,", "start": 379.28, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "thus fulfilling the aspirations of the", "start": 381.759, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "Sudin people, alleviating their", "start": 383.44, "duration": 3.199}, {"text": "humanitarian suffering and enhancing", "start": 385.039, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "their security and stability. The", "start": 386.639, "duration": 3.521}, {"text": "kingdom supports all efforts aimed at", "start": 388.479, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "strengthening Syria's security and", "start": 390.16, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "stability and preserving its territorial", "start": 391.759, "duration": 3.921}, {"text": "integrity. The kingdom welcomes the", "start": 393.52, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "USA's announcement of removing Syria", "start": 395.68, "duration": 3.519}, {"text": "from the list of states sponsoring of", "start": 397.44, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "terrorism in view of its contribution to", "start": 399.199, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "strengthening stability and", "start": 401.12, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "reconstruction and development.", "start": 403.199, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "And we have to um condemn and reject any", "start": 406.16, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "effort at the undermining effort to", "start": 409.84, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "restore security and stability within", "start": 411.68, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "Syria. In Lebanon, the kingdom", "start": 413.84, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "reiterated support for the Lebanese", "start": 415.919, "duration": 3.441}, {"text": "state and its legitimate institutions,", "start": 417.68, "duration": 2.959}, {"text": "the implementation of the Tarif", "start": 419.36, "duration": 3.04}, {"text": "agreement, the restriction of arms to", "start": 420.639, "duration": 2.96}, {"text": "the state and preservation of its", "start": 422.4, "duration": 2.96}, {"text": "sovereignty, security and stability. We", "start": 423.599, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "also attach importance to Iraq's role in", "start": 425.36, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "promoting cooperation and stability in", "start": 427.759, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "the region and support all effort to", "start": 429.44, "duration": 3.199}, {"text": "contribute to achieving security and", "start": 431.199, "duration": 3.681}, {"text": "stability and prosperity.", "start": 432.639, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "And we have to ensure that weapons will", "start": 434.88, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "only be restricted to the state to", "start": 437.52, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "ensure security and stability in Iraq.", "start": 440.0, "duration": 3.599}, {"text": "We have to ensure that the Iraqi", "start": 442.4, "duration": 2.48}, {"text": "territory will not become a source of", "start": 443.599, "duration": 2.961}, {"text": "attack against other neighboring", "start": 444.88, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "countries. Mr. President, the", "start": 446.56, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "achievements made through Saudi vision", "start": 449.44, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "2030 10 10 years after its launch", "start": 451.199, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "represent a model of comprehensive", "start": 454.16, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "national transformation. The latter is", "start": 455.84, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "based on economic diversification,", "start": 458.24, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "investment in human capital, promotion", "start": 460.16, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "of innovation, empowerment of youth and", "start": 461.84, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "women, development of the private sector", "start": 464.0, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "and consolidation of sustainability. The", "start": 466.16, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "vision has contributed to strengthening", "start": 468.319, "duration": 3.681}, {"text": "the kingdom's position as a region and", "start": 470.24, "duration": 3.359}, {"text": "international hub for business", "start": 472.0, "duration": 3.12}, {"text": "investment, tourism, industry,", "start": 473.599, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "technology, and logistics. Thus, uh,", "start": 475.12, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "nonoil activities accounted for 55% of", "start": 478.24, "duration": 7.679}, {"text": "non-oil GDP. The level of unemployment", "start": 482.0, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "among Saudis has declined, reaching 6.4%", "start": 485.919, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "in 2026, compared with 12.3%", "start": 488.96, "duration": 7.84}, {"text": "in 2016. Mr. President energy security", "start": 492.56, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "rests on the strength and resilience of", "start": 496.8, "duration": 3.519}, {"text": "the energy system and its capacity to", "start": 498.56, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "withstand and adapt to disruptions.", "start": 500.319, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "Uh ensuring the stability of energy", "start": 503.199, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "supplies, protecting critical", "start": 505.039, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "infrastructure, diversifying supply", "start": 506.639, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "roots, and safeguarding freedom of", "start": 509.12, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "navigation are all a shared", "start": 510.72, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "responsibility that require sustained", "start": 512.959, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "international cooperation. The kingdom", "start": 514.88, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "demonstrated this commitment in practice", "start": 516.959, "duration": 2.96}, {"text": "during the disruptions affecting", "start": 518.64, "duration": 2.879}, {"text": "maritime navigation through the street", "start": 519.919, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "of Harmos, maintaining the continuity of", "start": 521.519, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "energy supplies through its long-term", "start": 524.159, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "investments in infrastructure.", "start": 526.8, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "The East West pipeline together with its", "start": 530.48, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "petroleum reserves outside the region", "start": 533.279, "duration": 3.521}, {"text": "also contributed to mitigating the", "start": 535.2, "duration": 2.96}, {"text": "effects of those disruptions and", "start": 536.8, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "enhancing the reliability of supplies to", "start": 538.16, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "global markets. The kingdom affirms that", "start": 540.64, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "energy security and climate action are", "start": 543.2, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "mutually reinforcing objectives. U in", "start": 545.279, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "this context we stress the importance of", "start": 548.8, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "not excluding any source of energy and", "start": 550.48, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "of pursuing realistic and comprehensive", "start": 552.72, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "transition pathways that achieve energy", "start": 554.8, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "security, protect the climate and", "start": 556.88, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "support economic development. This", "start": 558.88, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "approach has contributed to making the", "start": 561.12, "duration": 2.8}, {"text": "kingdom one of the countries with the", "start": 562.56, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "lowest carbon and methane emissions", "start": 563.92, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "globally from hydrocarbon resource", "start": 566.64, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "production operations. The kingdom", "start": 568.56, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "continues to develop a more efficient", "start": 571.6, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "and sustainable energy system through", "start": 574.48, "duration": 3.12}, {"text": "the deployment of emissions reduction", "start": 575.92, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "technologies including carbon capture", "start": 577.6, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "utilization and storage and carbon", "start": 580.0, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "dioxide removal. We've also expanded the", "start": 582.399, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "use of renewable energy, the application", "start": 584.64, "duration": 3.12}, {"text": "of innovation, and the production of", "start": 586.48, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "sustainable fuels including clean", "start": 587.76, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "hydrogen. These efforts support energy", "start": 590.08, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "security, enhance resource efficiency,", "start": 592.32, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "and contribute to achieving", "start": 594.56, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "sustainability. Mr. President", "start": 596.0, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "the uh in light of the rapid", "start": 599.12, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "developments the world is witnessing in", "start": 601.92, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "the field of regional and international", "start": 604.16, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "trade there is need for um ensuring", "start": 608.0, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "continuous trade influx", "start": 611.44, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "especially from the east to the west.", "start": 615.04, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "This will not only be in um the support", "start": 617.519, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "of the kingdom but the world at large.", "start": 620.32, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "We have provided logistic support to the", "start": 622.64, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "neighboring countries during the current", "start": 624.72, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "um crisis by opening up our ports for", "start": 626.8, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "the transport of goods and people. This", "start": 629.68, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "um reflects our responsibility towards", "start": 632.399, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "the uh region and the world. In light of", "start": 635.92, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "the rapid developments the world is", "start": 638.959, "duration": 2.88}, {"text": "witnessing in the field of artificial", "start": 640.48, "duration": 3.039}, {"text": "intelligence, the kingdom stresses the", "start": 641.839, "duration": 2.961}, {"text": "importance of harnessing these", "start": 643.519, "duration": 2.88}, {"text": "technologies in the service of humanity", "start": 644.8, "duration": 3.12}, {"text": "and development and enhancing", "start": 646.399, "duration": 3.361}, {"text": "international cooperation to ensure the", "start": 647.92, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "responsible use.", "start": 649.76, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "The kingdom has taken a leading role in", "start": 651.839, "duration": 3.361}, {"text": "establishing the international network", "start": 653.519, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "of artificial intelligence capacity", "start": 655.2, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "building centers. One of the", "start": 657.279, "duration": 3.281}, {"text": "recommendations emanating from the pact", "start": 658.72, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "for the future. The kingdom also hosts", "start": 660.56, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "the international center for research", "start": 662.64, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "and ethics in AI in Riyad under the", "start": 664.399, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "opices of UNESCO thereby strengthening", "start": 667.36, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "international cooperation in this field", "start": 669.839, "duration": 3.761}, {"text": "and contributing to the consolidation of", "start": 671.6, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "ethical principles governing the", "start": 673.6, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "development and use of AI applications.", "start": 675.519, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "In conclusion, our world today is in", "start": 678.16, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "need of the greatest possible measure of", "start": 681.04, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "wisdom, responsibility, and cooperation.", "start": 683.76, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "The challenges confronting us cannot be", "start": 686.64, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "addressed by any state on its own.", "start": 688.8, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "Security can only be consolidated and", "start": 691.839, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "sustained through adherence to the", "start": 694.399, "duration": 3.601}, {"text": "principles upon which the UN charter is", "start": 696.0, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "founded as well as through a respect for", "start": 698.0, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "international law. The kingdom will", "start": 700.0, "duration": 3.04}, {"text": "continue to work with its partners in", "start": 701.6, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "the international community to advance", "start": 703.04, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "sustainable development, peaceful", "start": 705.04, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "solutions to crisis, and every pathway", "start": 706.88, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "that reinforces stability and builds", "start": 709.519, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "confidence based on mutual respect with", "start": 711.6, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "a view to building a safer and more", "start": 714.16, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "prosperous future for the region and the", "start": 716.32, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "world. Peace, mercy, and blessings of", "start": 718.399, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "God be upon you.", "start": 720.32, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "I thank the Minister for Foreign Affairs", "start": 723.44, "duration": 7.72}, {"text": "of Saudi Arabia.", "start": 727.12, "duration": 4.04}]